cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "NeuroBranch: leakage-safe C. elegans dynamics and bounded virtual-perturbation evaluation"
abstract: >-
  NeuroBranch is a research platform for C. elegans whole-brain population
  dynamics, latent branching and model-dependent virtual perturbation. Version
  1.4.0 replaces the Phase 11 0.560 headline with a three-estimand reliability
  audit: R_obs = 0.2606 at observed animal counts, R_22 = 0.3006 as a
  counterfactual for 87 of 126 targets, and R_id = 0.3501 on the identified
  subset. The historical 0.560 value is an extrapolated point estimate, not a
  bound. The animal-half extrapolation and target-ranking gates fail; no
  calibrated interval, ranking, animal budget or causal claim is published.
  Phase 14's zero-inflated model remains rejected. Intervention outputs are
  model-dependent and are not causally validated.
authors:
  - name: "NeuroBranch contributors"
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
keywords:
